  "cells": [
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "# Lab 1 — Heartbeat\n\nWelcome to your first **LoT (Language of Things)** notebook!\n\nIn Coreflux, an **Action** is a small event-driven rule that runs directly inside the broker. Every Action has:\n- A **trigger** — when it runs (for example, `ON EVERY 5 SECONDS DO` or `ON TOPIC \"...\" DO`).\n- A **body** — what it does (here, `PUBLISH TOPIC` sends a message to an MQTT topic).\n\n### How to run this lab\n1. Click the **▷ (Run / Deploy)** button on the code cell below to deploy `Heartbeat` to the broker.\n2. Open **Data Viewer** from the **bottom Dock**.\n3. Look for `campus` → `weather` → `heartbeat` in the topic tree and watch `\"ok\"` arrive every 5 seconds."
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE ACTION Heartbeat\nON EVERY 5 SECONDS DO\n    PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/heartbeat\" WITH \"ok\"\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "**Next up:** Open **`02-model-processweather.lotnb`** in the left sidebar to turn raw weather JSON into a clean, structured reading."
    }
  ]
}
